From a3fdc635827409a86212f49bb2122d5d93de18c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Bernhard M. Wiedemann" <bwiedemann@suse.de>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:48:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Port kNN and GUI buffer handling to Python 3.13

Python 3.13 removed the old buffer API: PyObject_CheckReadBuffer,
PyObject_AsReadBuffer and PyObject_AsWriteBuffer.  Add
include/pycompat.hpp with copies of CPython's own 3.0-3.12
implementations on top of PyObject_GetBuffer, and use them on every
Python version so there is a single code path.

GAMERA_PyObject_CheckReadBuffer probes PyBUF_SIMPLE like the original
instead of only testing for a buffer slot (PyObject_CheckBuffer), so
non-contiguous exporters are still rejected up front.

gui_support's get_writable_buffer ignored AsWriteBuffer's result and
then read an uninitialized pointer for read-only buffers; check it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gamera-4/include/knnmodule.hpp           |  7 +--
 gamera-4/include/plugins/gui_support.hpp | 16 ++++---
 gamera-4/include/pycompat.hpp            | 56 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 gamera-4/src/knncore/knncoremodule.cpp   | 11 ++---
 4 files changed, 77 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 gamera-4/include/pycompat.hpp

